FastAPI is initialized to create the backend API for the application. Required libraries are imported first, followed by the creation of the FastAPI application instance. The API can then define routes and handle client requests.
from fastapi import FastAPI
from pydantic import BaseModel
from typing import Optional

# Initialize FastAPI application
app = FastAPI(
    title="My Application API",
    description="Backend API for the application",
    version="1.0.0"
)

# Sample request model
class User(BaseModel):
    name: str
    email: str
    age: Optional[int] = None

# Root API endpoint
@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {
        "message": "FastAPI application is running"
    }
Running the Application
Use Uvicorn to start the FastAPI server:
uvicorn main:app --reload
The API will be available at:
http://127.0.0.1:8000
FastAPI also provides automatic API documentation at:
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
This gives you the initialization, required imports, API instance, sample model, route, and local deployment command in one section.
